WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.970
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:46.220
SPEAKER: Please welcome Diane
Greene, Senior Vice President,

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.520
Google Cloud.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.520
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:57.400
DIANE GREENE: OK.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.710
Welcome, everybody.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:00:59.960
Thanks so much.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:06.420
So many familiar faces-- on
behalf of our entire Google

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.380
Cloud executive team, we
want to welcome you here,

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.880
our customers, our partners,
and everybody else.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.230
We're pretty excited to
give you this September 29

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:20.390
snapshot of where we are.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:23.190
40 weeks-- we're
counting by the week.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:27.860
So much is happening that when
we brought this whole team

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:33.000
together as one, we're
really functioning as a team.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.750
And I'm sure I've talked to
over 200 customers and partners,

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:41.390
and I've learned a lot
from their customers

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.660
and our partners
about the unique value

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.890
that Google's bringing,
and I want to really

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:50.530
talk about that to you today.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:53.510
It's been a wonderful discovery.

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:56.600
And I also want to talk
to you about the fact

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:59.240
that when I came in, we
were Google for Work.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.100
We were GCP.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.300
We were Google Apps.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:07.110
We were the enterprise
mobile devices and so forth.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.620
And we go around,
talk to the customers,

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:15.490
and I'd be there with our
top technology people,

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.720
and we blow our customers away.

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:19.670
And we get to the end
of the conversation,

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:23.080
and I'd say, so,
any other questions?

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:26.160
And they'd go, yeah,
is Google really

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.425
serious about the enterprise?

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:34.420
And it was driving us
crazy because we're very

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.240
serious about the enterprise.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.670
It's why we were all there.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.810
And so we said,
well, maybe we better

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.980
call ourselves
Google Enterprise.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.880
So we started doing
that internally.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.610
We started doing it externally
just to put a point on-- we

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:51.780
are serious about
the enterprise.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.290
And then, a couple
of months ago,

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:56.320
all of a sudden the questions
started dissipating.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.560
People seemed to be getting it.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.330
Yep, they're putting their
money where their mouth is.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.090
They're serious
about the enterprise.

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.400
They're executing.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.310
They're delivering these things.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:09.350
And we're like, enterprise?

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:10.305
That was so June.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:16.650
We're the full power
of Google in the cloud.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.110
We're Google Cloud,
and that's what

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.430
our entire organization is.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:26.580
It's a uniquely Google broad
set of technology solutions,

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.750
products, all built
for the cloud,

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:36.870
from the Android and secure
Chromebook, enterprise mobility

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:42.590
devices, desktop devices, to
all of Google Cloud platform,

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:47.630
from the data centers up
through our data analytics,

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:52.430
the APIs, the machine learning,
the smart data that we make

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:58.190
available to our developers, the
maps APIs for the enterprise,

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:03.150
and our much loved, amazing,
built for the cloud,

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:06.000
completely integrated
collaboration

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:12.680
and productivity suite of tools
known as Google Apps-- changing

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.810
the name today.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.410
All of this is Google Cloud.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:21.440
And I have to say, when we said
this to everybody at Google,

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:23.140
there was just no questions.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:26.090
Everybody cheered, let
out a sigh of relief.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:29.960
Everybody feels that
we're Google Cloud.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:35.650
And this is-- I came to
work on Google Cloud.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.620
I knew it was just
a gigantic thing.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.080
But it's the biggest
IT transformation ever.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.500
What I didn't
appreciate was the pace.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:47.130
I have never seen
anything like it.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:51.610
The pace is just relentless, and
it's getting faster every day.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:55.360
And the totally amazing
thing given this pace

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.610
is where we are.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:58.260
We're at the beginning.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:03.190
So Deutsche Bank took the top
three public cloud vendors,

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:06.330
AWS, Google, and
Azure, and added up

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:09.020
their estimated
revenues and then said,

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.600
well, the IT
industry is something

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.000
more than $1
trillion, and it gets

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:18.720
5% of the total available
market is where we are today.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.210
So we're moving fast.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:24.440
We've got well over 10,000
engineers working on all this.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:28.000
Since January, 339
product releases,

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.840
including things like
new data centers,

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:35.520
new data analytics
functionality, search

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:41.710
functionality for the apps, and
so forth-- these next numbers

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:44.230
are our growth and revenue.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:47.890
So storage-- I recently
heard that there's

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:51.200
a new health company
startup that's

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:56.610
looking at two petabytes per
patient that they want to keep.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:59.430
Unbelievable numbers of
satellite images coming down.

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:03.280
You name it, storage,
revenue, 10x.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:07.450
Compute 4x-- and
we've really enjoyed

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:12.640
this unprecedented historical
bumping compute we've recently

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:17.640
had, where we've scaled up this
phenomena of all these zombies

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:20.650
walking around into fountains
and so forth, Pokemon

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:28.570
Go in a matter you'll hear
later from them about that.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:33.850
And then, a whopping 25x growth
in managed containers-- this

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:35.780
is how people are building apps.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:38.250
Developers are
building applications.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.250
It's fast.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.890
It's simple.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:44.010
You can concentrate on the
user-facing functionality

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:47.120
and let Google take
care of everything else.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:47.840
Very exciting.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.750
You'll hear more about that too.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:52.970
And then, finally,
we've always done really

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.020
well with consumers,
really well with

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:56.990
small, medium-sized businesses.

00:06:56.990 --> 00:07:00.520
And we really wanted to bring--
Google is one of the bigger

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.830
enterprises in the
world, and we are

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:08.910
100% on our suite of
productivity and collaboration

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.380
tools, Google Apps.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:13.460
And we said, let's bring this.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:19.570
Let's really show companies all
over the world, big companies,

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:21.730
how this can transform
their business

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:24.580
and really help them move
faster and more collaboratively

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.120
and more transparently.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:28.070
So we pushed for
big customers, which

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:31.450
we defined as more
than 5,000 seats,

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.540
and we're seeing 3x growth.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.570
So it's very exciting to us.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:39.070
And that includes
over 300,000 seats,

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:42.190
several over
100,000 seats, a lot

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:46.270
of big customers-- very happy.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:48.420
So the cloud-- how did it start?

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:50.936
Well, initially, it
was a convenient way--

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:52.310
if you were a
startup, you didn't

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:55.980
have to buy equipment,
servers, storage.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:59.160
If you were a department
that couldn't get resources

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.190
from your IT group,
you'd use the cloud.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:05.120
And people were trying to
figure out if they were really

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.620
saving money.

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:10.440
The smaller you were, the
more money you would save.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:14.410
And then something
happened where we started

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.625
getting all these breaches.

00:08:16.625 --> 00:08:19.470
A medical record
per patient costs

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:24.290
several hundred dollars
anywhere there's a breach.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:27.000
We all see all these
breaches, and it

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:30.550
started dawning on
people that you really

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:35.970
need scale to do security,
and so that's in the cloud.

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:41.690
So really, in boardrooms,
people started saying,

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:43.890
shouldn't you be looking
at saving some costs

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:46.450
and the security of the cloud?

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:49.100
I can't tell you
how many contacts

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:53.380
I get from people interested
in hiring a board member that

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:54.920
has cloud expertise.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:59.840
It's become mission critical to
companies to understand that.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:03.150
And everybody's
looking at moving.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.970
I sometimes wish the
pace would slow down.

00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:09.200
And so that's good.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.450
That's fine.

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.810
But the really
interesting thing going on

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:15.250
is the digital
transformation, what's

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:18.870
happening with people
becoming digital businesses.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.100
And I'll give you an example.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.720
If you think about
something like maps,

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:27.640
we all used to go to the AAA
and get our paper map before we

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:30.190
went off in our car on a trip.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:34.070
And it got digitized.

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:36.160
It went into the cloud.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:38.570
And what that did
was really provide

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:41.730
a platform for all kinds
of new business models,

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:43.070
all kinds of new services.

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:44.780
For instance, Waze
figured out they

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:48.470
could take real-time
traffic information

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:50.880
and overlay it on the maps.

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:53.300
What a phenomenal
value to customers.

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:55.200
Whole new business,
whole new set

00:09:55.200 --> 00:10:00.750
of value-- becoming digital
lets people move fast and let's

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:04.150
them get real-time data and
make real-time decisions.

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:07.560
It's completely
transformational.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:10.060
And every day, new
technologies are coming out

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:11.720
that let you do it
better and better

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:12.937
and do it more powerfully.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:18.780
What that all says is if you're
going to move to the cloud, who

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:22.960
your partner is really matters.

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:26.080
You want someone
that really is bold,

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.520
that's thinking
long term, that's

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.970
built for innovation,
that's going to keep you

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:34.490
on that innovation curve
so that you can compete

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:40.770
and have the latest empowering
technology right away, easily

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:43.260
and simply.

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:44.840
And I love this photo.

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:47.100
When I went to give this
talk, it was my first slide.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:50.735
I said, I want this slide in my
talk because I like the ocean.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:55.560
And this is US Faster.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:58.940
This is a submarine
cable laying ship,

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:00.870
and what it's doing
there in that picture

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:05.950
is we laid a cable from
9,000 kilometers from the US

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:12.250
to Japan, repeaters every
60 kilometers to energize--

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:15.070
re-energize the light.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:16.890
60 terabit per second.

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:22.620
That's, I think, 10
million or 100 million.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:26.380
I always keep getting these
orders at 10 million times more

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:28.650
capacity than a cable modem.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:34.250
Anyhow, the point is,
this is a big investment.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.840
Google has the best
network in the world.

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:40.190
It's estimated we run 30%
of the world's internet.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:43.110
It's been publicly
estimated that we run

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:46.270
30% of the world's internet.

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:48.670
We reach everywhere
in the world,

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:54.120
difficult to reach places
like Saudi Arabia, Africa.

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:57.979
We have to for our
7 billion plus apps.

00:11:57.979 --> 00:11:59.520
And actually, I'll
digress once more.

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:03.780
We recently figured out
because of our customers

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:08.060
that actually Google has 8
billion plus active user apps

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:11.310
because Google Cloud and
its users are clearly

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:14.330
over a billion active users.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:16.600
But anyhow, so the
point is, you want

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:19.790
someone that innovating,
that's thinking long term,

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:20.838
and moving forward.

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:27.910
This is a very exciting thing.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:28.960
Google knows this.

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:31.270
I didn't fully
assimilate it until we

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:35.200
were talking to a customer
of ours, a big SAS vendor.

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:36.660
And they kept asking questions.

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:39.420
Well, what happens if
the network goes down?

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:41.860
And well, how does
that identity work

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:45.600
in all the different
places in your system?

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:48.730
And then finally, this
CIO/CTO looked at us

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:51.370
and he said, do you know what?

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:55.870
Google actually has the most
enterprise appropriate approach

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.530
of any cloud.

00:12:58.530 --> 00:13:03.370
And what that is, is
when we build something,

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.910
we think of it as a system
not as a bunch of components

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:10.530
that you, the user, have
to assemble and hope it

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:14.570
all has the same availability.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:16.360
But if you're doing
data analytics

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:17.970
and the network
goes down, you can't

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:19.440
get at your data analytics.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:20.540
You can't run it.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:26.000
And so anything that would keep
you from offering your service

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.730
is considered the
system at Google.

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:29.720
That's how we think.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:32.520
That's how we built
Google from the beginning.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.250
We had to.

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:39.900
And so what that means is,
also Google gets the cloud.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:43.290
Google was started in the cloud,
Google was built for the cloud.

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:45.620
And so we can even give
you a slider so you

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:49.050
can say, if I don't
want a high SLA,

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:52.930
if I don't want high
availability or performance,

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:55.460
it costs Google less
so your price is less.

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:59.460
If you want the five nines
and the lowest latency,

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:00.840
it costs you more.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.180
But we can slide that.

00:14:02.180 --> 00:14:05.390
And because we took the system
approach, we can do that.

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:07.050
I think it's a really big deal.

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:16.620
Google does have
the best security.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:21.350
We have over 600 people, we
do keep our customers secure.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:25.710
However, our customers need
to convince their customers

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:28.240
and they need to
convince the regulators

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:29.700
that they are secure.

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:33.060
So what that means is we're
working with our customers

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:37.030
to knock off all the compliance
badges that they need

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:40.450
to work with the regulators
together with our customers

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:44.130
all over the world
and help them prove

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:49.530
to the people they need to prove
it to that they are secure.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:54.830
Huge effort here, one we
embrace very heartily.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:58.020
And then machine learning.

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:01.420
Something Google invested in
pretty much from the beginning.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:07.290
Today at Google we have a
phenomenal community of machine

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:09.410
learning and AI researchers.

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:12.920
We have Google Brain, we
have the alphabet companies,

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:16.810
Deep Mind, Verily, now Calico.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:18.730
We have Google Cloud ML.

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:22.430
All those research
scientists, a huge assemblage

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:25.500
of the world's best, working
together as a community

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:28.160
to move the state
of the art forward.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:31.670
And what we're so excited
about with Google Cloud

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:33.000
is we can democratize it.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.690
We can bring it to everybody.

00:15:35.690 --> 00:15:38.120
Google Brain open
source tenser flows

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.840
so that everybody could do it.

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:43.640
And now we're increasingly
building the tools

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:45.820
to make it easy for
any of our customers

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:48.850
to take their own proprietary
data and train it.

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:55.150
We also bring our smart data,
if you will, our training data,

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:57.710
and let you query
it through APIs.

00:15:57.710 --> 00:16:00.960
You can read text.

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:05.290
You can recognize address.

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:11.930
You can do speech recognition
and so forth through the APIs

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:13.560
Direct to Developers.

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:16.260
And of course, all
of Google's products,

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:20.250
as you'll hear from Prabhakar in
our suite of productivity apps,

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.390
are infused with
machine intelligence.

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:29.950
And speaking of machine
learning-- so in addition,

00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:33.270
we're going to have a nice
cross-section of our customers

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:35.500
today to tell you
how they're using it.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:42.280
Airbus using image
recognition to detect clouds.

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:46.400
Home Depot, who is also using
our recently acquired company

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:51.900
Apogee-- hasn't quite closed
yet-- to do the API management.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:54.360
They're using Google Cloud
and the API management

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:57.000
to make it easy for them
to talk to their customers

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.190
and partners.

00:16:58.190 --> 00:17:01.750
And then Telus International,
the Canadian-- well,

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:06.770
international telco-- 20,000
people all over the world

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:09.140
using Google Apps and Chrome.

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:10.900
And then in a
different category,

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:18.710
we have Snap, formerly Snapchat.

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:22.746
And I think I get more excited
than my 18-year-old daughter

00:17:22.746 --> 00:17:24.579
now when they do a new
release because we're

00:17:24.579 --> 00:17:25.790
provisioning for it.

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:31.160
And then we'll have
Pokemon Go talking

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:33.090
about their recent debut.

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:39.280
And then finally, Evernote,
which was on-prem,

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:40.840
has been on-prem.

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:44.020
They recently decided
to move to the cloud.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:47.650
We were pretty excited
to win the bake off.

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:51.030
Their CEO will be
here telling you why.

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:55.340
And we also are pretty
excited about-- we deeply

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:59.230
embrace partnering at
Google and Evernote is one

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:03.960
where partnering deeply around
Google Apps for the benefit

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:05.890
of our mutual customers.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.300
We've also got
pure partners here.

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:11.730
We have Pivotal making it
easier for our developers

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:14.860
to quickly build apps agilely.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:18.590
We have many, many partners
here in the audience-- PWC

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:19.560
and Accenture.

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:22.910
The CTO of Accenture is here
to announce our partnership

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:25.070
with them and talk
about what he's seeing.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.835
Stepping back,
what's going on here?

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:36.810
Google's been having huge impact
on the world right from the

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.180
get go.

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:42.160
But we kind of think
with the late 2013

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.140
release of Google
Compute Engine,

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.480
we kind of moved
into the exponent.

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:48.160
It's great to be
in the exponent.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:49.700
It's leverage.

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:51.580
And the reason we
have that leverage

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:53.860
now is it's not just us.

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:56.050
It's why we're
the eighth billion

00:18:56.050 --> 00:19:01.520
plus active user sort
of app at Google.

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:03.880
With our customers,
with our partners,

00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:06.900
we're having an exponential
impact all over the world.

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:09.300
We think bringing
our technology,

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:12.720
getting our customers
on our technology curve,

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:15.530
it's actually going to spur
economies all over the world.

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:19.000
The small startup in
Africa has the best

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:20.530
of Google's machine learning.

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:22.640
They can do image
recognition, they

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.890
can do language
translation, they

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.620
can use everything we have.

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:30.080
And so they can concentrate
on their great ideas

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:32.640
and getting it into the
market very quickly.

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:35.590
This is unprecedented,
these kinds of capabilities

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:37.370
for everybody in the world.

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:40.950
And that's what gives us
this exponential impact which

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:44.160
we're all very excited about.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:47.050
And so today you're
going to hear

00:19:47.050 --> 00:19:50.900
from the rest of our Google
Cloud team, our executives,

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:53.100
with announcements
about some new products

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:56.920
that we have in
all kinds of areas,

00:19:56.920 --> 00:20:01.480
and then also our
customers, our partners.

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:03.530
And so I'm going to wrap up.

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:06.030
And I just want to
kind of summarize

00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:09.280
three big things of what I've
been talking about today.

00:20:09.280 --> 00:20:12.890
One is just the excellence
of our engineering

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:16.380
and how important this
systems approach is.

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:21.255
I also want to really emphasize,
when you sign up to the cloud,

00:20:21.255 --> 00:20:22.040
it's a bet.

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:23.370
It's a long term bet.

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:28.410
In fact, I have had
two customers now that

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:30.770
want to evaluate Google Cloud.

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:32.360
And one of them
in particular said

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:34.160
that they were kind of
looking for a reason

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:39.380
not to look at Google Cloud, who
wants to learn something new.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:42.480
And they couldn't
find it, and then they

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:45.102
caucused among themselves.

00:20:45.102 --> 00:20:46.310
And they said, you know what?

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:47.450
We've decided.

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:51.650
We've decided, in five years,
Google will have won this.

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:53.130
Google will have won this.

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:54.220
I can barely say it.

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:55.280
It makes me so happy.

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:57.430
[LAUGHTER]

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:02.152
And it's because of
the technology curve

00:21:02.152 --> 00:21:03.360
we're going to get people on.

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:04.950
And when you
compare our products

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.240
to our competitors'
products, apples to apples,

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:09.010
they're just plain better.

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:15.440
And we're closing the
gap incredibly fast.

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:18.620
And then, finally,
Google's about substance.

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:19.980
It's a technology company.

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:22.030
We want to partner
with our customers.

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:23.760
We want to make them successful.

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:26.750
We're merging two sets of
technology, our customers

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:30.130
and ours, and that requires
partnering and technical

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:31.330
interaction.

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:33.020
And that's what we're doing.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:35.260
And Tarik who leads
our customer facing

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:37.790
will tell you more about that.

